{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4723",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are subunits of the Nadh dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) complex, and these subunits are involved in the activity of Ndufv1. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to these subunits, which in turn participate in the activity of Ndufv1. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Metformin influences Ndufv1, likely through modulation of the Nadh dehydrogenase complex. The high scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and robust relationship, with Metformin acting as a modulator of the complex that ultimately affects Ndufv1. The mechanism is supported by the direct interaction of Metformin with the subunits and their role in the activity of Ndufv1, implying that Metformin may influence Ndufv1 through a pathway involving the Nadh dehydrogenase complex. The evidence is consistent and provides a clear, mechanistic link between Metformin and Ndufv1, supported by multiple paths with similar scores.",
